/* _ss_wfm for OS-9/68k -- SetStat SS_WFM, "write a tape file mark". * * It exists only in LIB/tape.l, and l68 rejects that file outright: "not a * relocatable module", the same as os_lib.l and ppplib.l.  So the symbol * cannot be linked on this disk at all. * * GNU tar reaches it in one place, diffarch.c, on the path taken when lseek * on the archive fails -- which is to say when the archive is a TAPE and has * to be rewound instead.  There is no tape here, and RBF has no SS_WFM. * * Returning -1 is what OS-9 does with a SetStat a device does not implement, * and it is what the caller is already written to handle: the line after it * tests _ss_rest() for ERROR and reports that it cannot rewind.  A stub that * returned 0 would claim a file mark had been written and be a lie. */int_ss_wfm(path, count)	int path;	int count;{	return -1;}